# Vue 3 + Storybook Standards

Follow [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md) and [docs/FRONTEND_CONVENTIONS.md](docs/FRONTEND_CONVENTIONS.md).

## Components

- Use `<script setup lang="ts">` always. No Options API or `defineComponent` for new components.
- Type props: `defineProps<Props>()` with interface; `withDefaults()` for defaults.
- Type emits: `defineEmits<{ eventName: [payload?: Type] }>()`.
- Use design tokens only (no magic numbers): `text-sm`, `p-4`, `gap-2` — not `text-[13px]` or `px-7`.
- Canonical reference: [src/modules/ui/components/InfoBanner/](src/modules/ui/components/InfoBanner/).

## Storybook

- Every UI component needs a `.stories.ts` file.
- CSF3 format: `Meta<typeof Component>`, `StoryObj<typeof Component>`.
- Include Default, Variants; States (Loading, Disabled, Error) only when component has those props. See [FRONTEND_CONVENTIONS](docs/FRONTEND_CONVENTIONS.md#storybook-standards).
- Use `args.children` for default slot in story templates (Storybook-only).

## Stores & Composables

- Pinia for cross-route/global state; composables for page/component logic.
- Use `storeToRefs` when destructuring store state in components.
